    <div>
      <h2 id="standards-title">The standards behind every job</h2>
      <p class="answer">Read the tree first, protect what's around it, cut in control, and clean up as if we were never there.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p><strong>Assessment before price.</strong> Certified arborists look at lean, decay, crown weight and the target before a number is given. That is how a quote stays accurate on the day of the work.</p>
      <p><strong>Rigging over guesswork.</strong> Near homes, trees come down in sections lowered on ropes or lifted by crane. Felling whole trees is reserved for open ground.</p>
      <p><strong>Honest recommendations.</strong> If pruning or cabling will make a tree safe, you'll hear that, even though removal is the bigger job.</p>
      <p><strong>Cleanup is part of the job.</strong> Chipping, hauling, raking and blowing are included, not an add-on at the end.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{{ ctaBlock("Want an arborist's opinion on a specific tree? Ask on the phone.", "Same day service for most visits.", business) }}

